  "details": "Steps to reproduce: \n\n1. Join world that uses Audio Reverb Zone, and enter the Audio Reverb Zone\n\n2. Get remote user with an avatar that has Audio\n\n3. configure Safety Settings so you should not hear that audio\n\n4. have remote user play avatar audio\n\nbugged result: you cannot hear the audio, but you can hear the REVERB of the audio from the Audio Reverb Zone\n\nexpected result: you cannot hear the audio at all\n\nextra notes:\n\n1. I have only tested this on PC. I do not know about other platforms, but I suspect this bug is platform-agnostic. However, I have only marked PC due to lake of evidence.\n\n2. I do not know whether or not adding VRC Spatial Audio Source component to the avatar's audio source would fix this, but that component is not expected nor mentioned anywhere ever (not even once) so I suspect most avatars with audio do not have it, meaning it's an issue regardless. If i had tested more thoroughly, I would have made test cases both with and without VRC Spatial Audio Source on the avatar's audio source. \n\nAttached is footage of this happening in-game! I remembered to record something for once. yippee.",
